From a85e9f45fbd6b8fbb6d1ed72d1f4bf80ee5e748f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Craterbrain <58347640+Craterbrain@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 20:43:46 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] soong_ui: plan the build from the memory that is free now

Soong sizes its parallelism from total RAM ("32 GB or less: 2 memory-heavy
jobs"), whatever else is running. On a 30 GB desktop that already holds 10+ GB
(idle pages swapped to zram), a full ROM build drove memory and swap past the
90% swap line at which systemd-oomd kills the whole build, four times in a row.

The build's memory budget is the available RAM (MemAvailable) minus
(100 - ceiling)% of the total minus an optional extra reserve. The ceiling is
2 points under systemd-oomd's SwapUsedLimit when oomd is running (read from
oomd.conf and its drop-ins in systemd's order), else 88%. If less than 4 GiB
of swap is left before the kill line (oomd's limit, or 95% without oomd), the
budget shrinks by the shortfall. From the budget come the default -j (about
2.5 GiB per job, never above cpus+2), the number of memory-heavy jobs (about
10 GiB each, 1 or 2) and soong_build's GOMEMLIMIT (85% of the budget, whole
GiB, 8 to 24 GiB). An explicit -j, NINJA_HIGHMEM_NUM_JOBS, a smaller
GOMEMLIMIT or GOMEMLIMIT=off always wins; remote builds keep Soong's
highmem rule. The decision is printed at the start, with a warning when the
budget is under 8 GiB.

soong_build runs with env -i, so GOGC/GOMEMLIMIT never reach its Go runtime
at startup. Putting them in its ninja command would make every new value
re-run the whole analysis, so soong_build applies them itself
(debug.SetGCPercent/SetMemoryLimit) from the available-environment file,
which is read without dependency tracking (like LOG_DIR).

  PLAIT_MEM_BUDGET=off        stock behavior
  PLAIT_MEM_CEILING_PCT=88    the ceiling, 50..98 (overrides the oomd one)
  PLAIT_MEM_RESERVE_GB=0      extra memory left to everything else

Linux only (/proc/meminfo); no change on macOS. The calculation is in
ui/build/memory_budget.go, the Go settings in shared/gomemory.go, both with
unit tests (including one that soong_build's command has no memory settings).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
